2026-06-19 13:14:43,512 | AGENT | SecurityCompliance Agent answered: Based on our company context, we can implement several measures to ensure the security and compliance of our proposed solution. Firstly, as an ISO 27001 certified company since 2023, with a scope that includes development, delivery, and operations, we have a robust information security management system in place to protect sensitive health data. 

Additionally, our ISO 27701 certification for privacy information management extension ensures that we have the necessary controls to handle personal data securely. We also hold HDS certification for health-data hosting through OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified sovereign cloud infrastructure, ensuring that our processing on this infrastructure is covered and compliant with relevant health data regulations.

To protect sensitive health data, we can implement encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and encryption at rest using AES-256. We also use EU-based infrastructure for key management, ensuring that encryption keys are securely managed within the EU. Furthermore, we can apply pseudonymisation where relevant to further protect sensitive health data.

Our experience with GDPR delivery, particularly for public-sector and health clients including special-category (Art. 9) health data, demonstrates our capability to handle sensitive health information in compliance with GDPR requirements. We are familiar with frameworks such as CNIL guidance, HDS reference framework, and HAS guidance on AI in healthcare, which guides our approach to ensuring the security and compliance of our solution.

In terms of AI security controls, we have a secure software development lifecycle (SDLC) that includes code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, and periodic penetration testing by an external CREST-equivalent provider. We also have defined remediation SLAs by severity for vulnerability management and incident response plans in place, including breach notification procedures within 72 hours.

Our solution's audit logging capabilities, configurable retention policies, and tenant isolation with strict logical separation between client corpora further contribute to the security and compliance of our proposed solution. With a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed and a data processing register in place, aligned with GDPR Art. 28, we ensure that all data processing activities are properly documented and compliant.

Lastly, our experience with control mapping links platform features to applicable obligations, providing audit evidence available for regulatory scrutiny. By leveraging these measures and our extensive experience with EU regulatory frameworks, including GDPR and the upcoming EU AI Act, we can ensure the security and compliance of our proposed solution, addressing the client's requirements for strict GDPR compliance, data sovereignty, and protection of sensitive health data.
